* fhevm whitepaper v3.1 vs code
** Four principles
*** No impact on host chain security
*** Exact, publicly verifiable results
*** Solidity and existing tools
*** Composable, multi-user confidentiality
** Components and trust
*** Host contracts (ACL) trusted
*** Coprocessors: > 1/2 honest, slashable
*** KMS: > 2/3 honest, 13 parties, t = 4
*** Gateway: orchestrator, no trust
*** Oracle and relayer: none, signed messages
** Solidity library (paper)
*** ebool, euint, eint, ebytes, eaddress
*** select for branching
*** fromExternal + attestation
*** allow / allowTransient / allowForDecryption
*** Oracle-based public decryption
*** User decryption with EIP-712 token
** Implementation details (paper)
*** TFHE, programmable bootstrapping
*** Handles: hash(op, inputs), state independent
*** Inputs: packed ZKPoK, 1.3 s / 130 ms / 1.8 kB
*** Commitments: d_req and d_sns
*** t+1 public, 2t+1 user shares
*** NIST lifecycle, custodial backup
** Changes in the repository
*** Oracle removed: self-relaying decryption
*** MultichainACL removed: KMS reads host ACL
*** Types restricted: no eint, no ebytes
*** Handles mix blockhash, timestamp, chainId
*** Added: fees, contexts, delegation, pausing
** Still future
*** Verifiable FHE
*** Post-quantum ZKPoK
*** Verifiable KMS, threshold signatures
@endmindmap
